<body>

<!-- HEADER -->
<div class="header">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="header-badge">&#9632; Equity Research &nbsp;|&nbsp; Historical Analysis</div>
    <h1>Nike Inc. <span>(NKE)</span> Historical Stock Performance</h1>
    <div class="header-sub">26-Year Capital Markets Review &mdash; January 2000 through January 2026</div>
    <div class="header-meta">
      Data: {first_date} &ndash; {last_date} &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; {6559:,} Trading Days &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; Adjusted Closing Prices &nbsp;&bull;&nbsp; Source: Kaggle / NKE Daily OHLCV
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="container">

<!-- SECTION 1: EXECUTIVE SUMMARY -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">01</span>
    <span class="section-title">Executive Summary</span>
  </div>

  <!-- KPI Dashboard -->
  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card green">
      <div class="kpi-label">Cumulative Return</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">+{cumulative_return:,.0f}%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">{first_date} &rarr; {last_date}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card blue">
      <div class="kpi-label">CAGR</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">{cagr:.1f}%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Annualized over {n_years:.0f} years</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card red">
      <div class="kpi-label">Max Drawdown</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">{max_dd:.1f}%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">{max_dd_peak} &rarr; {max_dd_trough}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card purple">
      <div class="kpi-label">Annualized Volatility</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">{annualized_vol:.1f}%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Std dev of daily returns &times; &radic;252</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card gold">
      <div class="kpi-label">Avg Daily Volume</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">{avg_volume_m:.1f}M</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Mean shares/day (2000&ndash;2026)</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="info-row">
    <div class="info-card">
      <div class="info-card-label">All-Time High</div>
      <div class="info-card-value">${ath:.2f}</div>
      <div class="info-card-sub">{ath_date}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-card">
      <div class="info-card-label">All-Time Low (Adj.)</div>
      <div class="info-card-value">${atl:.3f}</div>
      <div class="info-card-sub">{atl_date}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-card">
      <div class="info-card-label">Starting Price</div>
      <div class="info-card-value">${first_close:.4f}</div>
      <div class="info-card-sub">{first_date}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-card">
      <div class="info-card-label">Latest Price</div>
      <div class="info-card-value">${last_close:.2f}</div>
      <div class="info-card-sub">{last_date}</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="exec-text">
    <p>Nike Inc. (NYSE: NKE) delivered a <strong>cumulative return of +{cumulative_return:,.0f}%</strong> over the 26-year period from January 2000 to January 2026, equating to a <strong>CAGR of {cagr:.1f}%</strong> — meaningfully above long-run equity benchmarks. A $10,000 investment at the start of 2000 would have grown to approximately <strong>${10000 * (1 + cumulative_return/100):,.0f}</strong> by January 2026, ignoring taxes and transaction costs.</p>
    <div class="exec-highlight">
      Nike's compounding story unfolded in three distinct epochs: <strong>a volatile recovery decade (2000–2009)</strong> with +200% cumulative gain, <strong>a dominant growth decade (2010–2019)</strong> producing +597% — the engine of long-term wealth creation — and <strong>a reversal phase (2020–2026)</strong> that saw shares pull back 34% from their pandemic-era peak, driven by inventory normalization, demand uncertainty in key markets, and multiple earnings disappointments.
    </div>
    <p>The stock reached an <strong>all-time high of $166.25 on November 5, 2021</strong>, before entering a prolonged correction. The deepest drawdown on record was <strong>-68.5%</strong>, measured from the ATH to the trough of April 2025. Despite this, the stock's adjusted price bottomed at <strong>$2.468 in February 2000</strong>, underscoring the transformative scale of Nike's long-term price appreciation. Best performing year: <strong>{best_year} (+{ann_dict[best_year]:.1f}%)</strong>. Worst: <strong>{worst_year} ({ann_dict[worst_year]:.1f}%)</strong>.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 2: PRICE TREND -->
<div class="section">
  <div class="section-header">
    <span class="section-num">02</span>
    <span class="section-title">Long-Term Price Trend Analysis</span>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-card">
    <div class="chart-title">NKE Monthly Closing Price — Full History (2000–2026)</div>
    <div class="chart-sub">Adjusted closing price; logarithmic scale highlights compound growth structure</div>
    <canvas id="priceChart"></canvas>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-row" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
    <div class="chart-card" style="margin-bottom:0;">
      <div class="chart-title">Drawdown from All-Time High</div>
      <div class="chart-sub">Running peak-to-trough percentage decline</div>
      <canvas id="drawdownChart"></canvas>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-card" style="margin-bottom:0;">
      <div class="chart-title">Rolling 90-Day Annualized Volatility</div>
      <div class="chart-sub">63-trading-day window, sampled every 5 days</div>
      <canvas id="volChart"></canvas>
    </div>
